    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d615-a3">

                <pb facs="1082" n="988" xml:id="pg988"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 to inclosure in No.
                    180.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Williams to Messrs. Lawton Brothers.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate-General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Havana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-02-18"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 18,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: As this office is now called upon
                    several times a day by American citizens for its official aid to obtain
                    passports for them to leave the island, after having been admitted here without
                    that document, and who allege that you refuse to issue them tickets to return to
                    the United States by the American steamers to your consignment only upon the
                    previous delivery to you of a passport issued by the civil government, and as I
                    have to report and explain the matter to my Government, I will esteem it a
                    particular favor if you will have the goodness to furnish me a copy of the
                    instructions you may have received from the authorities upon the subject,
                    whether written or Verbal.</p>
                <p>I remain, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ramon O. Williams</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Consul-General.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
